    "src/routes/[[preview=preview]]/about/+page.svelte": {
      "alt\tHeadshot of ${…}, ${…}": 3,
      "button\tHide Bio": 6,
      "button\tShow Bio": 6,
      "copy\tAbout Espada": 1,
      "copy\tBrent Conlin": 1,
      "copy\tBrent is a commercial real estate developer and private equity investor with 30+ years in professional real estate experience predominantly in San Antonio and South Texas. As a Managing Partner of Espada, he oversees development and investment activities. He has served as Managing Partner of Espada Real Estate (formerly Reata Assets, Investments & Development) since its inception in 2012, after more than a decade of corporate real estate experience at the Trammell Crow Company. Brent has a BBA and a MS in Land & Real Estate Development from Texas A&M University. He serves on the ULI San Antonio Advisory Council and is a member of the San Antonio Real Estate Council and ICSC. Brent is a Co-Captain of the Valero Texas Open Trailblazers and an Executive Committee Member of the Development Industry Advisory Council for the Texas A&M graduate program in land & property development.": 1,
      "copy\tContact Card": 2,
      "copy\tDon Thomas": 1,
      "copy\tDon is a commercial real estate broker, developer, manager and equity investor in properties, restaurants and other operating businesses. Prior to co-founding Espada Real Estate and joining CBRE in 2019, Don co-founded Reata Real Estate Services in 2001. Prior to Reata, Don was a Partner/ Principal for The Trammell Crow Company for thirteen years. Don’s responsibilities include leasing, property management, development, acquisition and disposition. Don’s commercial real estate activity spans San Antonio, Austin, Dallas/ Fort Worth and Tulsa, OK. Don earned a BBA from Texas Christian University and currently serves on multiple nonprofit boards.": 1,
      "copy\tEspada Real Estate evolved from Reata Assets Investment and Development (RAID) after the sale of the Reata companies to CBRE in 2019. The founders of RAID, now Espada, collectively have 140 years of experience in the retail real estate industry and have worked with former companies such as Trammell Crow, CBRE, and United Commercial Realty. In more recent years, Espada partners and their associates have developed and acquired other notable projects including Sonterra Village, Dominion Springs Plaza, St. Paul Square, Brooks Corner, Memorial Crossing, Baytowne Shopping Center and Rio Norte shopping center. The name Espada, Spanish for “sword”, speaks to the company’s partners’ long history in San Antonio. The name pays tribute to Mission Espada, the oldest Spanish mission in Texas and one of the five missions in San Antonio that were recently designated as a World Heritage Site.": 1,
      "copy\tJohn Wright": 1,
      "copy\tJohn is a commercial real estate developer, and investor. After nearly 10 years as a commercial broker focused on the representation of retail tenants and landlords at Trammell Crow Company and CBRE, John joined Reata Real Estate’s development and investment team where he was responsible for identifying opportunities, sourcing debt and equity and overseeing the execution of projects. At Espada, John is focused on building a portfolio of real estate assets that produce superior risk- adjusted returns. John has a BA from Wake Forest University and an MBA from The Owen Graduate School of Management at Vanderbilt University.": 1,
      "copy\tKaitlin Davey": 1,
      "copy\tKaitlin is the Property Manager St. Paul Square, Patriot Plaza, and Live Oak Shopping Center. She is currently managing a portfolio of about 1,000,000 square feet of Class A office and retail space. Prior to joining Espada Real Estate, Kaitlin worked in commercial property management for Spigel Properties where her portfolio was comprised of shopping centers with a strong concentration in Michigan, Ohio and Texas. Kaitlin is an active member of IREM San Antonio. Kaitlin earned her BA from Texas Tech University.": 1,
      "copy\tKathy Palmer": 1,
      "copy\tKathy has 25+ years of experience as a Chief Financial Officer and Accounting Manager, specializing in commercial real estate and property management, in San Antonio and South Texas. Kathy has a BBA in Accounting from the University of Texas at Arlington.": 1,
      "copy\tMichael Jersin": 1,
      "copy\tMicheal is a commercial real estate developer, investor, broker, and equity investor in operating real estate projects and businesses. Prior to joining CBRE, Michael held leadership roles as CEO at Reata Real Estate (acquired by CBRE) and President of United Commercial Realty – San Antonio. With 30 years of experience in the commercial real estate industry, Michael has led many successful real estate developments, redevelopments and repositioning of commercial assets. His current role with Espada Real Estate is the co- manager of the Espada owned assets and the pursuit of commercial real estate opportunities. At CBRE, Michael will continue to serve his clients in the greater San Antonio and suburbs of San Antonio market. Michael has a Bachelor of Business Administration from the University of Texas at San Antonio and a Master of Science from Trinity University.": 1,
      "copy\tMitch Nichols": 1,
      "copy\tMitch is a commercial real estate developer, investor, broker, and private equity investor. After 25 years in the medical device sales industry, he joined ESPADA in 2018. In his role as Director of Medical Development he is responsible for identifying, underwriting, financing and executing development and investment opportunities. Mitch has a Bachelor of Science Degree from Angelo State University. He is an active member in the Urban Land Institute of San Antonio and the Real Estate Council of San Antonio.": 1,
      "copy\tThomas Tyng": 1,
      "copy\tThomas is a commercial real estate broker and investor with 30+ years of experience in tenant representation, project leasing and investment sales. Prior to co-founding Reata Real Estate Services in 2001, Thomas worked for three years at The Woodmont Companies in Fort Worth and for nine years at Trammell Crow Company in San Antonio. After the sale of Reata Real Estate Services to CBRE, Thomas and his Espada partners formed Espada Real Estate where his responsibilities include acquisitions, leasing oversight and assisting in asset management. At CBRE, Thomas will continue to serve clients in San Antonio, Austin, Laredo, Corpus Christi and the Rio Grande Valley. Thomas received his BBA from Texas Christian University.": 1,
      "heading\tDevelopment and Investment Team": 1,
